cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CDFD Runtime, cite this software release. Cite the separate Part I–IV scholarly archives only when you use those manuscript materials directly."
title: "CDFD Runtime: Constraint-Driven Flux Dynamics and CDFL Execution Engine"
version: "1.1.1"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20343160
date-released: 2026-08-25
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/bampita-bico/CDFD-Runtime"
authors:
  - family-names: Mujjabi
    given-names: Steve Bico
    name-suffix: MD
    affiliation: Vura Labs
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0556-5516"
abstract: "Slim public command-line runtime for Constraint-Driven Flux Dynamics and CDFL. The active release provides deterministic CLI execution, CDFL lint/format/AST tooling, runtime finite-audit helpers, one canonical example model, one reproducible smoke experiment, VS Code CDFL language support, and focused tests. Outputs are deterministic toy-model diagnostics and software-audit artifacts, not empirical evidence, calibrated forecasts, or deployed decision systems. A new versioned deposit is required before citing v1.1.1 by DOI."
keywords:
